"[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408084} {:answer/id #uuid "5305f733-f1f5-5fee-a5d0-db365d37810d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408085} {:answer/id #uuid "adb0e76d-9986-5b8e-a736-d4821798cae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408091} {:answer/id #uuid "efb8a5b6-21b1-5345-9b9e-e436922d4029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408096} {:answer/id #uuid "feae4636-ed31-53a4-b5a1-dfde035b20cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408097} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb9eed7-da79-5b44-8508-0e1881d8523f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38a55885-c791-5e66-b4d4-e155d750a7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130322" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d768f671-89dc-5731-b1ab-0bc434b2394f"}] :activity/title "Quiz 3" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408076}]}
